<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Foster's settles Elliott case.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Foster's settles Elliott case.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia wine and brewing company Foster's Brewing Group Ltd said on Friday it had settled civil proceedings against former managing director John Elliott and other former directors.</p>
<p>&quot;Foster's Brewing Group advises that it has agreed to the striking out of the civil proceedings against the former directors, Messrs Elliott, Scanlon, Biggins and Jarrett, the Bank of New Zealand and against Price Waterhouse,&quot; Foster's said.</p>
<p>&quot;The terms of the settlement between the parties, which was determined by mediation, remain confidential&quot;, it said.  </p>
<p>The A$66.5 million civil claim by Foster's against BNZ and the former executives sought to recover funds used in two foreign exchange deals in 1988 and paid to New Zealand businessman Allan Hawkins.</p>
<p>-- Melbourne bureau 61-3 9286-1435</p>
</text>
